ws Leonard even, and Democratic outside groups are investing, so the race is closer than a typical incumbent hold without reaching true tossup territory.", "watch": "Whether independent or Republican-sponsored polling confirms the September Hart result, and whether national Democratic spending scales up in the final weeks.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Incumbent Mike Carey (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Mike Carey seeks a third term in this Columbus-area Republican-leaning district, facing Democrat Don Leonard, a former Ohio State professor. Carey holds a decisive financial edge, with roughly $2.1 million on hand to Leonard's $250,000, and the seat's R+5 lean favors the incumbent. Most expert raters call the race Likely Republican, though a few see it as Lean R or even a Tossup.\n\nThe race has tightened in polling: Democratic-sponsored Hart Research showed Leonard trailing by four points in August but tied at 46-45 in late September. Headlines highlight Democratic attacks on Carey over cuts to SNAP, Medicaid, and education, and national Democrats have run ads in the district. Prediction markets still price Carey as a clear favorite, and the balance of evidence points to a Republican win with real but limited risk.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.1732, "margin": -5.63}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.185, "margin": -6.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.1905, "margin": -6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.1541, "margin": -7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.1527, "margin": -6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.1532, "margin": -6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.1445, "margin": -7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.1885, "margin": -6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.341, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.336, "margin": -3.0}]}